comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T22:12:37.531Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: searched every status for GH-956, remove-ac unmatched behavior, replace-only --ac, and acceptance-criteria loss. Closed pm-xh82 deliberately added exact-match warnings and replace-then-add composition; #956 proves the remaining destructive combination, while pm-inn5y5 concerns branch merge storage, so this is distinct follow-on work."
  "2026-08-10T08:26:22.857Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: acceptance-criteria replacement is mutually exclusive with additive selectors; every unmatched removal returns structured NOT_FOUND before persistence; remove+add repairs are atomic; replacement emits count receipts; update-many dry-run and apply share validation. Focused tests, clean-directory failure-atomic acceptance, and the full 7141-test suite pass."
  "2026-08-10T08:36:14.542Z","harness:codex","Hosted static-gate feedback disposition: regenerated the aggregate contract fixture so acceptance_criteria_mutation_conflict and acceptance_criteria_remove_unmatched are visible in canonical CLI contracts."
  "2026-08-10T08:46:00.516Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit feedback implemented: update-many is explicitly attributed as an acceptance_criteria_mutation_conflict emitter in the generated catalog; shared create/plan acceptanceCriteria wording no longer advertises unsupported addAc/removeAc fields, while update actions retain atomic repair guidance."
  "2026-08-10T08:53:29.546Z","harness:codex","Review-fix verification: generated aggregate contracts are current; update-many error attribution and action-scoped acceptanceCriteria descriptions are covered by focused tests and the exact 100/100/100/100 repository coverage run."
